     "andreas_1885_v2"
    ],
    "note": "The 1871 plan's streets north of North Avenue are unnamed. Hurlbut Street is taken as the plan's north-south street at about local E -227 (about 500 west on the later numbering, the place Cleveland Avenue holds), and Linden Street as its east-west street at about local N 2949 (about 1700 north, Eugenie Street's). The church's north-west corner is set on their south and east building lines, its front on Linden Street and its long side on Hurlbut Street, as the engraving shows the front and the long side meeting at a street corner. The footprint's origin is local E -216.14 N 2878.85.",
